
README on nova-core:
********************

nova-core is a rust implementation of a core driver to init and talk to the NVIDIA GSP processor and provide some core services for other drivers. Other drivers are currently considered to be vGPU and nova-drm driver in the future.

This tree also has the nova-c driver which is a port of nouveau to nova-core API. This is currently only accelerator support, no display code has been ported as this point.

Config Options:
===============

This branch has

CONFIG_NOVA_CORE - this enables the core driver support
CONFIG_NOVA_CORE_VGPU_SUPPORT - this enables the basic features for the VFIO driver (CONFIG_NVIDIA_VGPU_VFIO_PCI) to talk to. Do *NOT* enable this option if you want to use nova-c

CONFIG_DRM_NOVA_C - this enable the NOVA_C driver. DO NOT ENABLE THIS AND THE VGPU SUPPORT, if you do you will get wierd RC TRIGGERED when you use the graphics engine

Code layout:
============

nova_c.rs, driver.rs: boilerplate, utils and bindings to pci/aux

nvfw/ - autogenerated GSP interface handling

dma.rs: objects to handle coherent dma allocations used in various places
bios.rs: lowlevel BIOS parsing, used to find fwsec
devinit.rs: memory sizing, devinit waiting
rm_riscv.rs, firmware.rs: lowlevel firmware header parsing and loaded firmware storage
timer.rs: handle the GPU timer
falcon.rs, sec2.rs: base and sec2 falcon handling for loading and executing fws (used by gsp)
vfn.rs: handle the vfn interrupt controller

gpu.rs:
=======
This is the main GPU driver object implementation. There are two GPU objects, GpuBase and Gpu, GpuBase contains the initial phase of setup (per-gpu info, bios, timer, pci bar). This is used to bring up the other pieces of the main Gpu structure.

The main Gpu struct contains, interrupt and event handlers, bar, mmu, instance memory and a few other objects, along with main gsp struct.

This sets the basic GPU functions up, boots GSP, sets up BAR1/2 VM handling, and inits the GR golden context.

GSP:
====

mod.rs is the main GSP handling code flow. It contains the main abstraction for different versions of GSP, inside the GspManager trait. This is the API, everything below this API can access the versioning abstractions, and all versioned info should be inside the gsp subdir.

gsp bringup does all the memory sizing, sysmem flush, fwsec load, shared memory, shared queue, msg setup, boot then queries a bunch of GSP info and adds the irq handler.

boot_structs.rs: memory sizing struct fillers and libos struct fillers
fwsec.rs: fwsec handling
gsp_falcon.rs: the GSP falcon handling
sharedq.rs: has all the shared memory queue handling, contains all the msg passing functions, 
notifiers.rs: has all the handling for callbacks from GSP events (cpu sequencer, rc trigger)
msgs.rs: lowest level rpc msg handling
rpc_msgs.rs: the VGPU MSG handling
alloc_msgs.rs: all the msgs inside GSP_RM_ALLOC msgs
ctrl_msgs.rs: all the msgs inside GSP_RM_CONTROL msgs

Accel:
======

The accel dir has the FIFO and GR handling.

fifo.rs has chid allocation, fifo device struct handling, channel handling
gr.rs has GR golden context and context promotion handling

mmu:
====

mm.rs: this is a direct port of the nouveau mm.c range manager, it probably could be done a lot nicer
mmu.rs: mmu physical page table handling and heap/type handling
memory.rs: physical memory handling, these all share a trait interface, just not sure if that helps or not.
   - VramObj - VRAM objects
   - InstObj - Instance memory wrapper around vram object
   - DmaMemObj - DMA memory object
   - SglMemObj - TODO
   
vmm.rs: this is a port of the nouveau vmm.c but missing raw handling and sparse handling and I think needs rustification. The raw handling should more likely be done at the higher level or via a completely separate API.
mm

API:
====
exports.c: workaround for rust EXPORT_SYMBOL issues

vgpu_mgr.rs: provides a C API mostly compatible with the VGPU RFC

include/drm/nova_core_if.h:
core_api.rs:
These provide the C API to the nova-c driver, these are a very much torn down version of the nouveau driverif, all direct calls, very little indirection, this file mostly translates the rust<->C struct handling and has a lot of the unsafest code.


nova-c:
=======
This is mostly nouveau code with the nvif layer ripped out and replaced with direct nova-core calls. This is considered a test vehicle until we can write a nova-drm driver.
